<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  macOS entitlements for the Sovrium app SHELL: the Tauri executable and the
  .app bundle around it. Tauri signs both with this file, under the hardened
  runtime (bundle.macOS.hardenedRuntime defaults to on).

  It is empty on purpose. The shell is compiled Rust and runs no JIT of its
  own; the web view's JavaScript engine runs in WebKit's separate web content
  process, which carries Apple's entitlements rather than ours. So the shell
  needs none of the runtime exceptions, and every one it held would weaken the
  process that owns the window and the permissions macOS grants the app:
  turning library validation off, or honouring the dynamic loader environment
  variables, would let another program load code into it.

  The engine sidecar is the one binary that needs exceptions (JavaScriptCore is
  a JIT). It is signed with its own file, entitlements.plist beside this one,
  and is kept out of Tauri's signing pass so that file is not overwritten: see
  desktop/tauri-cli.ts.

  Add a key here only for a capability the shell itself uses (for instance the
  microphone, if the window ever records audio), with the reason next to it.

  NOTHING IN THIS COMMENT MAY CONTAIN TWO CONSECUTIVE HYPHENS: AMFI, the parser
  inside codesign, rejects the whole file for it, while plutil accepts it.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict/>
</plist>
